   "locked": false,
   "text": "Step by step: one \"Run test\"\n\n①  The tester types a goal in plain words, picks a\n    version and presses Run test → POST /api/run.\n    (Guided demo → POST /api/demo: the same journey\n    4 times: A from scratch → B → B with bug → B.)\n\n②  The web app deploys that version of the shop on\n    its ONE private address and clears the order store.\n\n③  The typed-intent builder (plain code) reads the\n    shop catalogue and the test data (card, address,\n    phone) from intents/checkout.json.\n\n④  Same words as a saved intent? → replay the\n    recorded AI answers (offline, same every time).\n    A new sentence → the live AI plans it.\n\n⑤  It writes runs/typed/<id>.json: goal + inputs +\n    a success check written by CODE (1 new order,\n    product, price, card last 4). No AI here.\n\n⑥  runIntent() loads and lints it, and splits it:\n    the healer view (goal + input names, NO success\n    check) and the verifier view (the success check).\n\n⑦  The verifier counts the orders BEFORE anything\n    is clicked (the baseline).\n\n⑧  The planner reuses runs/plans/<id>.json if it has\n    one; otherwise the strong AI turns the goal into\n    milestones (cart → checkout → shipping → payment\n    → place order). Steps are filled in on each live\n    screen.\n\n⑨  The executor opens Chromium (headed, slowMo 300)\n    on the shop and walks the milestones, skipping\n    any already done, within action and time budgets.\n\n⑩  For every step the ladder finds the element:\n    1 saved locator → 2 name similarity (code) →\n    3 the fast AI picks 1 of 8 candidates →\n    5 the strong AI re-plans the milestone (max 2).\n\n⑪  Playwright clicks / fills on the real app. Each\n    action must make progress; a heal is kept only if\n    it worked, then saved in runs/locators/<id>.json.\n\n⑫  The final \"Pay / Place order\" click runs exactly\n    once, then the run goes straight to the verifier.\n\n⑬  The verifier (code only, never the AI) reads the\n    real order store: exactly 1 new matching order?\n    its id on the page? no error alert?\n    → GREEN · AMBER (passed after healing) · RED · GREY\n\n⑭  The reporter writes runs/<time>-<id>/ (events,\n    verdict, report.html, pr.md, screenshots). For a\n    RED real bug the fast AI adds a \"likely cause\"\n    (narration only: the verdict is already final).\n\n⑮  Every event streams live to the page (SSE);\n    the result card shows verdict, summary, what\n    changed, and a link to the full report.\n\nSecond run of the same goal: plan + locators are\nsaved, so it usually needs 0 AI calls.",
   "originalText": "Step by step: one \"Run test\"\n\n①  The tester types a goal in plain words, picks a\n    version and presses Run test → POST /api/run.\n    (Guided demo → POST /api/demo: the same journey\n    4 times: A from scratch → B → B with bug → B.)\n\n②  The web app deploys that version of the shop on\n    its ONE private address and clears the order store.\n\n③  The typed-intent builder (plain code) reads the\n    shop catalogue and the test data (card, address,\n    phone) from intents/checkout.json.\n\n④  Same words as a saved intent? → replay the\n    recorded AI answers (offline, same every time).\n    A new sentence → the live AI plans it.\n\n⑤  It writes runs/typed/<id>.json: goal + inputs +\n    a success check written by CODE (1 new order,\n    product, price, card last 4). No AI here.\n\n⑥  runIntent() loads and lints it, and splits it:\n    the healer view (goal + input names, NO success\n    check) and the verifier view (the success check).\n\n⑦  The verifier counts the orders BEFORE anything\n    is clicked (the baseline).\n\n⑧  The planner reuses runs/plans/<id>.json if it has\n    one; otherwise the strong AI turns the goal into\n    milestones (cart → checkout → shipping → payment\n    → place order). Steps are filled in on each live\n    screen.\n\n⑨  The executor opens Chromium (headed, slowMo 300)\n    on the shop and walks the milestones, skipping\n    any already done, within action and time budgets.\n\n⑩  For every step the ladder finds the element:\n    1 saved locator → 2 name similarity (code) →\n    3 the fast AI picks 1 of 8 candidates →\n    5 the strong AI re-plans the milestone (max 2).\n\n⑪  Playwright clicks / fills on the real app. Each\n    action must make progress; a heal is kept only if\n    it worked, then saved in runs/locators/<id>.json.\n\n⑫  The final \"Pay / Place order\" click runs exactly\n    once, then the run goes straight to the verifier.\n\n⑬  The verifier (code only, never the AI) reads the\n    real order store: exactly 1 new matching order?\n    its id on the page? no error alert?\n    → GREEN · AMBER (passed after healing) · RED · GREY\n\n⑭  The reporter writes runs/<time>-<id>/ (events,\n    verdict, report.html, pr.md, screenshots). For a\n    RED real bug the fast AI adds a \"likely cause\"\n    (narration only: the verdict is already final).\n\n⑮  Every event streams live to the page (SSE);\n    the result card shows verdict, summary, what\n    changed, and a link to the full report.\n\nSecond run of the same goal: plan + locators are\nsaved, so it usually needs 0 AI calls.",
   "fontSize": 18,
